# ── Reiwa OS environment ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reiwa OS runs on hosted Supabase: Supabase Auth for identity and Supabase
# PostgreSQL for data. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values from
# your project's dashboard. All four variables are required.

# ── Supabase HTTP API (Auth / PostgREST) ────────────────────────────────────
# Project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Publishable ("anon") key — safe in the browser; RLS is what protects the data.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Secret ("service") key — SERVER ONLY. Used solely by the Admin API to
# provision Supabase Auth accounts during seeding. Never expose to a client.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Supabase PostgreSQL (privileged, RLS-gated at the session level) ────────
# Connection string for the transaction pooler (port 6543), e.g.
#   postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# This credential is kept strictly separate from the API keys above.
DATABASE_URL=

# Optional — the Supabase pooler certificate is issued by Supabase's own CA,
# which is not in the public trust store. The root is shipped at
# supabase/prod-ca-2021.crt and used automatically; set this to a PEM string or
# an alternative path to override it. TLS verification is always enabled.
# SUPABASE_DB_CA_CERT=

# Optional — local connection pool size (default 8).
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=

# ── Automated tests: a SEPARATE, DISPOSABLE database ────────────────────────
# The integration suite DROPS EVERY APPLICATION TABLE on every run. It reads
# this variable and only this one — there is no fallback to DATABASE_URL, and
# naming the same database in both is refused.
#
# Point it at a separate Supabase project you would not mind losing. NEVER
# reiwa-dev, staging or production.
#
# The target database must also identify itself, on its own account, both as
# the test project and as destroyable. These are properties of the database
# rather than of its name, and neither implies the other:
#
#   ALTER DATABASE postgres SET app.environment = 'test';                -- what it is for
#   ALTER DATABASE postgres SET app.destructive_reset_allowed = 'true';  -- may be destroyed
#
# `npm run db:reset -- --yes` requires the second marker on DATABASE_URL too:
# --yes says you meant to type the command, not that it is aimed at the right
# database. NEVER put that marker on reiwa-dev while it backs a live-facing
# deployment or holds data anyone would miss.
#
# Full instructions: docs/19-test-database-safety.md
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# The destructive opt-in. Required for `npm test`, NOT for `npm run test:e2e`.
# Set it per run on the command line:
#
#   ALLOW_TEST_DATABASE_RESET=true npm test
#
# Deliberately NOT set here: a flag that authorises dropping every table should
# be typed each time, not inherited from a file. Leave it commented out.
# ALLOW_TEST_DATABASE_RESET=

# ── Outbound application email (investor invitations) ───────────────────────
# SERVER ONLY. Resend API key, used by the "Send invitation" admin action to
# email the secure /access/<token> link to an investor contact.
#
# This is NOT the same channel as the one-time codes: those are sent by
# Supabase Auth through the project's own SMTP settings, which give this
# application no ability to send mail of its own.
#
# The sender identity is Reiwa Capital <invitations@reiwa-capital.com>
# (src/lib/email/send.ts); that domain must be verified in Resend.
#
# Without it the portal runs normally and only "Send invitation" is refused,
# with a clear message. Never give this a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# SERVER ONLY. The canonical investor portal origin, used to compose the
# /access/<token> link in invitation emails. Production:
#
#   INVESTOR_PORTAL_URL=https://portal.reiwa-capital.com
#
# This is deliberately NOT derived from the request (Host, Origin,
# X-Forwarded-Host): those are client- or proxy-supplied, and a poisoned header
# would put a working invitation link to somebody else's domain into an
# investor's inbox, sent from Reiwa's own mail server.
#
# Validated at the point of use: https outside localhost, an origin with no
# path, query or fragment, trailing slash stripped. Like RESEND_API_KEY it is
# send-required, not boot-required — the portal runs without it and only
# "Send invitation" is refused. Never give this a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# INVESTOR_PORTAL_URL=
